    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0231" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg149"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Marsh</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 135.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 24, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of June 29, No. 123, has been
                    received. I thank you for the interesting information which it communicates. It
                    is not deemed important that you should make at present any proposition to the
                    Italian government relative to the negotiation of a consular convention. You
                    will, therefore, confine yourself, under the authority that has already been
                    given you, to the negotiation of a commercial treaty.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">George P. Marsh,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Florence.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
